GIVEN `transfer between districts approved by the supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has priority in the queue for work in the new district` `transfer between districts approved by the supervision` IF
    `transfer between districts approved by the supervision`

-- As the takanon's §6.17.12 (העברה להוראה) groups them:

-- 1: a permanent guide physically unable to do his duties is put, where
-- needed, before a pedagogical committee on his fitness to teach; not fit,
-- the Ministry applies to the Civil Service Commission. The text does not
-- say who puts him before the committee; the Ministry, which acts in the
-- next sentence, is read as the one (F-6.17-i).
-- att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_h__cls_3 here, against the takanon's §6.17's words: the takanon restates it in words a little its own.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_h__cls_3
GIVEN `permanent and physically unable to do his duties as a guide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `6.17 party` `6.17 action`
DECIDE `6.17.12.1 the pedagogical committee` `permanent and physically unable to do his duties as a guide` `needed` IS
    IF `permanent and physically unable to do his duties as a guide` AND `needed`
    THEN PARTY `the Ministry`
         MUST  `put the guide before a pedagogical committee that examines his fitness to teach`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Ministry` BECAUSE "6.17.12.1"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_h__cls_3
GIVEN `the pedagogical committee found him unfit to teach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `6.17 party` `6.17 action`
DECIDE `6.17.12.1 a guide unfit to teach` `the pedagogical committee found him unfit to teach` IS
    IF `the pedagogical committee found him unfit to teach`
    THEN PARTY `the Ministry`
         MUST  `apply to the Civil Service Commission to look for work for him in the civil service, by Takshir chapter 11.63`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Ministry` BECAUSE "6.17.12.1: not fit to teach"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_h__cls_4 here, against the takanon's §6.17's words: the takanon restates it in words a little its own.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_h__cls_4
GIVEN `the guide asks to be accepted as a teacher in an official institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `the supervision recommends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `6.17 party` `6.17 action`
DECIDE `6.17.12.2 a guide asking to become a teacher` `the guide asks to be accepted as a teacher in an official institution` `the supervision recommends` IS
    IF `the guide asks to be accepted as a teacher in an official institution` AND `the supervision recommends`
    THEN PARTY `the Ministry`
         MUST  `endeavour to grant the guide's request to be accepted as a teacher in an official institution`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Ministry` BECAUSE "6.17.12.2: as the possibilities of the time allow, subject to the law and regulations on employing teachers in official institutions"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples. Salaries are placeholders, not the takanon's.
`a matriculated certified guide` MEANS
    `guide schooling` WITH
        `years of schooling`                     IS 12
        `has a Hebrew matriculation certificate` IS TRUE
        `finished the Gadna guides' seminar`     IS TRUE
        `passed Gadna and its teaching`          IS TRUE
        `passed Shelach and its teaching`        IS TRUE
        `passed psychology`                      IS TRUE
        `passed Hebrew language`                 IS TRUE
        `positive supervision assessment for a year or more` IS TRUE
        `exams of the 1962 booklet still owed`   IS 0
        `the one exam owed is Shelach and its teaching` IS FALSE

`a 10-year guide with Shelach, psychology and Hebrew` MEANS
    `guide schooling` WITH
        `years of schooling`                     IS 10
        `has a Hebrew matriculation certificate` IS FALSE
        `finished the Gadna guides' seminar`     IS FALSE
        `passed Gadna and its teaching`          IS FALSE
        `passed Shelach and its teaching`        IS TRUE
        `passed psychology`                      IS TRUE
        `passed Hebrew language`                 IS TRUE
        `positive supervision assessment for a year or more` IS FALSE
        `exams of the 1962 booklet still owed`   IS 3
        `the one exam owed is Shelach and its teaching` IS FALSE

§§ `Property checks`

-- The section's rules over their whole finite space: guides at a half, a
-- full and a position and a quarter, with 0 to 12 frontal hours of 12, 24
-- or 30 weekly hours, reporting 0 to 6 preparation hours, the day before
-- and the day of 1.9.94; every schooling (9 to 12 years, the eight
-- booleans, 0 to 2 exams owed — 3,072 cases); 0 to 6 years of probation
-- and of work at every grade; 0 to 14 hours worked and owed; and every
-- mother (the four booleans, a child of 0, ½, 1, 1½, 2, 3 or 14 years).

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`every guide grade` MEANS
    LIST `certified teacher or higher`, `certified Shelach guide`, `non-certified Shelach guide, stage AA`,
         `non-certified Shelach guide A`, `non-certified Shelach guide B`

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER, fr IS A NUMBER, w IS A NUMBER, gr IS A `guide grade`
GIVETH A `Shelach guide`
DECIDE `a checked guide` f fr w gr IS
    `Shelach guide` WITH
        `position fraction`      IS f
        `frontal teaching hours` IS fr
        `weekly hours`           IS w
        `is on probation`        IS FALSE
        `is permanent`           IS TRUE
        `grade`                  IS gr
        `monthly salary`         IS 9000

-- 6.17.3 over every position fraction in quarters up to a position and a
-- half: a guide owes the full quota from a full position and a share of it
-- below, never more, never less with a larger position; the full-position
-- list binds exactly from a full position, and its IDF march and briefings
-- ask nothing of a part-time guide.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                LET f MEANS k DIVIDED BY 4
                    g MEANS `a checked guide` f 6 24 `certified Shelach guide`
                IN      `monthly field-day hours owed` g 100 AT LEAST 0
                    AND `monthly field-day hours owed` g 100 AT MOST 100
                    AND `monthly field-day hours owed` (`a checked guide` (f PLUS 1/4) 6 24 `certified Shelach guide`) 100
                        AT LEAST `monthly field-day hours owed` g 100
                    AND `the full-position list binds the guide` g EQUALS (k AT LEAST 4)
                    AND (`the full-position list binds the guide` g
                         OR (`6.17.3 א(4) the IDF march` g EQUALS FULFILLED AND `6.17.3 א(8) briefings and training` g EQUALS FULFILLED)))
            (range 0 6)

-- 6.17.4 over 0 to 6 years of probation and of work at every grade: tenure
-- always needs the supervision's finding; a certified guide or higher may
-- have it after 2 to 4 years of probation; any grade after 5 consecutive
-- years; and another year of work never takes it away.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN gr YIELD
                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                        all (GIVEN y YIELD
                                LET g MEANS `a checked guide` 1 6 24 gr
                                IN      NOT `entitled to tenure` g p y FALSE
                                    AND `entitled to tenure` g p y TRUE
                                        EQUALS (   (elem gr (LIST `certified Shelach guide`, `certified teacher or higher`) AND p AT LEAST 2 AND p AT MOST 4)
                                                OR y AT LEAST 5)
                                    AND ((NOT `entitled to tenure` g p y TRUE) OR `entitled to tenure` g p (y PLUS 1) TRUE))
                            (range 0 6))
                    (range 0 6))
            `every guide grade`

-- 6.17.5 over every schooling: the grade a guide is given is never lower
-- than another definition he meets would give, and passing one more exam,
-- or owing one fewer, never lowers it. F-6.17-h over the same space:
-- guides meet two definitions — certified and "non-certified A", "stage
-- AA" and "non-certified A".
GIVEN gr IS A `guide grade`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rank of` gr IS
    CONSIDER gr
    WHEN `certified teacher or higher`           THEN 4
    WHEN `certified Shelach guide`               THEN 3
    WHEN `non-certified Shelach guide, stage AA` THEN 2
    WHEN `non-certified Shelach guide A`         THEN 1
    WHEN `non-certified Shelach guide B`         THEN 0

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, mt IS A BOOLEAN, sm IS A BOOLEAN, gd IS A BOOLEAN, sh IS A BOOLEAN, ps IS A BOOLEAN, hb IS A BOOLEAN, ev IS A BOOLEAN, ow IS A NUMBER, os IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `guide schooling`
DECIDE `a checked schooling` y mt sm gd sh ps hb ev ow os IS
    `guide schooling` WITH
        `years of schooling`                     IS y
        `has a Hebrew matriculation certificate` IS mt
        `finished the Gadna guides' seminar`     IS sm
        `passed Gadna and its teaching`          IS gd
        `passed Shelach and its teaching`        IS sh
        `passed psychology`                      IS ps
        `passed Hebrew language`                 IS hb
        `positive supervision assessment for a year or more` IS ev
        `exams of the 1962 booklet still owed`   IS ow
        `the one exam owed is Shelach and its teaching` IS os

GIVEN prop IS A FUNCTION FROM `guide schooling` TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds for every schooling` prop IF
    all (GIVEN y YIELD
            all (GIVEN mt YIELD
                    all (GIVEN sm YIELD
                            all (GIVEN gd YIELD
                                    all (GIVEN sh YIELD
                                            all (GIVEN ps YIELD
                                                    all (GIVEN hb YIELD
                                                            all (GIVEN ev YIELD
                                                                    all (GIVEN ow YIELD
                                                                            all (GIVEN os YIELD prop (`a checked schooling` y mt sm gd sh ps hb ev ow os))
                                                                                `both booleans`)
                                                                        (range 0 2))
                                                                `both booleans`)
                                                        `both booleans`)
                                                `both booleans`)
                                        `both booleans`)
                                `both booleans`)
                        `both booleans`)
                `both booleans`)
        (range 9 12)

`a matriculated certified guide is also "non-certified A"` MEANS
        `is a certified Shelach guide` `a matriculated certified guide`
    AND `is non-certified A` `a matriculated certified guide`

`an 11-year guide owing Hebrew alone` MEANS
    `a checked schooling` 11 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE

-- F-6.17-g over 0 to 14 hours worked and 0 to 10 owed: 1.2's formula as
-- printed, the hours worked up to 10 less the hours owed, falls below zero
-- exactly where the roster owes more than that; the encoding pays nothing
-- then, and otherwise exactly the printed hours.
GIVEN w IS A NUMBER, o IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `1.2's hours as printed` w o IS min w 10 MINUS o

-- 6.17.8 over every mother: whoever is released from treks is released
-- from national service too; physical work is released exactly in
-- pregnancy; the pay rule of (5) holds exactly to a child under 14.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN pr YIELD
                all (GIVEN gb YIELD
                        all (GIVEN mo YIELD
                                all (GIVEN nu YIELD
                                        all (GIVEN a YIELD
                                                LET m MEANS `guide mother` WITH `is pregnant` IS pr, `gave birth` IS gb, `is a mother` IS mo,
                                                                            `child's age in years` IS a, `is nursing, with a medical certificate` IS nu
                                                IN      ((NOT (`released from` m)'s `treks`) OR (`released from` m)'s `national service`)
                                                    AND (`released from` m)'s `physical work` EQUALS pr
                                                    AND `pay computed as for teacher mothers of children under 14` m EQUALS (mo AND a LESS THAN 14))
                                            (LIST 0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, 2, 3, 14))
                                    `both booleans`)
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`

-- F-6.17-i's evidence: what 6.17.12.1's two sentences say, read off the
-- text. The first, putting the guide before the committee, names no one;
-- the second names the Ministry.
DECLARE `6.17.12.1 sentence` HAS
    `sentence`        IS A NUMBER
    `names who acts`  IS A BOOLEAN

`the sentences of 6.17.12.1` MEANS
    LIST `6.17.12.1 sentence` 1 FALSE, `6.17.12.1 sentence` 2 TRUE
